-## Meeting-to-action outcome
+## Consumed meeting-to-action and card contract
 
 ```text
-source evidence
-  -> canonical transcript segments with provenance/confidence/gaps
-  -> meeting-owned summary candidate + action candidates
-  -> participant/reviewer correction and approval
-  -> explicit task promotion through Product-Suite task authority
+source/capability adapters (this lane)
+  -> canonical meeting evidence with provenance/confidence/gaps
+  -> caller-authority PR B: meeting-owned summary/action candidates
+  -> caller-authority PR B: review and explicit task promotion
 ```
 
-All capture paths render the same compact post-meeting review pack. Each action candidate card shows a plain title, one-line reason/source, recommended next step, and `Add`, `Adjust`, or `Dismiss`. `Adjust` opens an inline agent conversation with at most two or three natural-language planning choices; every revision creates a new candidate version linked to its predecessor and evidence. Structured fields, confidence details, and provenance stay hidden until relevant, but remain inspectable and auditable.
+This lane consumes, but does not implement, the caller-authority PR B mixed-content card contract. Every candidate card has an icon/type, plain title, one-line source, up to three high-confidence chips or links, and `Add`, `Adjust`, or `Dismiss`. Missing or uncertain values are omitted rather than defaulted. `Adjust` opens an inline agent conversation with at most two or three natural-language planning choices; PR B versions every revision and keeps structured fields/provenance hidden until relevant.
 
-Action candidates contain proposed text, proposed owner, due date, evidence segment IDs, confidence, version lineage, and status (`draft`, `needs_review`, `adjusting`, `approved`, `dismissed`, `promoted`). `Add` is the explicit review approval that may invoke task promotion; it is never automatic. Promotion is idempotent and records reviewer, source candidate version, target task ID, and timestamp. Low speaker confidence, incomplete evidence, or ambiguous ownership forces `needs_review`; it never blocks preserving or adjusting the candidate.
+Only caller-authority PR B may define candidate versions, `Add`/`Adjust`/`Dismiss`, or promotion. `Add` is explicit review approval and is never automatic; `Adjust` and `Dismiss` create no task/work item. Connector evidence may supply optional source links/chip facts, but cannot choose their presentation or promote work.
 
 ## Recommended MVP sequence
 
-1. Lock the four boundaries and common evidence/output contracts.
-2. Ship explicit local microphone/tab capture as the first source, consuming the sibling durability protocol and showing mixed-audio speaker limitations.
-3. Produce the common compact review pack; require `Add`, versioned `Adjust`, or `Dismiss` before any task promotion.
+1. Land caller-authority PRs A/B, including canonical evidence authority and the mixed-content review contract.
+2. Land local durability issue `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a` and terminal-finalization issue `ce942338-35af-4960-ae83-ebc55bdbbe2a`; prove a real transcript/finalize E2E.
+3. Add the source capability/evidence adapter seam and local source projection without candidate or review writes.
 4. Add calendar recognition for meeting association, reminders, and capability preflight—never automatic recording.
-5. Integrate Recall as an explicit Zoom/Meet/Teams join fallback with conformance, consent, region, retention, availability, diarization, and budget checks.
-6. Pilot platform-native paths separately: Zoom RTMS first when its gates pass; Google Meet Media only after production availability; Teams native/compliance paths only for justified tenant use cases.
+5. Integrate Recall as an explicit Zoom/Meet/Teams join fallback with consent, region, retention, availability, diarization, and budget checks.
+6. Pilot platform-native paths separately: Zoom RTMS only when its gates pass; Google Meet Media only after production availability; Teams native/compliance paths only for justified tenant use cases.
 
