+OWASP implementation coverage: server-derived ACL inputs (A01); encrypted artifacts/secrets (A02); schema, size, URL, and webhook validation (A03/A04); deny-by-default consent/region/provider settings (A05); dependency scanning (A06); verified provider/OAuth identities (A07); hashed provenance and idempotent evidence ingest (A08); audit events without raw transcript/media (A09); and bounded concurrency/timeouts/circuit breakers (A10).
 
-Tests must cover cross-tenant metadata injection, missing/revoked consent, indicator loss, mixed-audio unknown speakers, low-confidence action ownership, duplicate/out-of-order evidence, incomplete transcripts, `Add`/`Adjust`/`Dismiss`, revision lineage, more than three adjustment choices, duplicate task promotion, calendar recognition without capture authority, provider capability drift, cost exhaustion, unsupported region, provider outage, and deletion pending/confirmed.
+This lane's tests cover cross-tenant metadata injection, missing/revoked consent, indicator loss, mixed-audio unknown speakers, duplicate/out-of-order evidence, incomplete transcripts, calendar recognition without capture authority, provider capability drift, cost exhaustion, unsupported region, provider outage, deletion pending/confirmed, and proof that no adapter writes candidates, proposals, tasks, or work items. Card actions, revision lineage, and promotion tests belong exclusively to caller-authority PR B.
 
